      "description": "Watch Marseille vs Strasbourg highlights and goals from Ligue 1 on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 21, 2026. The lights of Ligue 1 shone brightly on August 21, 2026, as Olympique Marseille welcomed Strasbourg for a clash defined by tactical patience and explosive moments. Both sides entered the pitch looking to establish dominance in a match that promised high-octane drama from the opening whistle. A Tense Tactical Opening The first half of this encounter was a story of missed opportunities and defensive resilience. Strasbourg showed early intent, with Samir El Mourabet and Sebastian Nanasi testing the Marseille backline through a series of corners. However, the hosts remained composed, as Emerson attempted to orchestrate play from the flanks. Despite the pressure from both sides, the final ball lacked the precision needed to break the deadlock, leaving the match finely poised as the teams headed into the interval. Gouiri Ignites the Flame The complexion of the game changed instantly at the start of the second half. Just seconds after the restart, Angel Gomes delivered a perfect pass to find Amine Gouiri , who clinically finished with his left foot to give Marseille the lead in the 46th minute. The momentum shifted heavily in favor of the home side, and the situation worsened for Strasbourg in the 59th minute when Samir El Mourabet was shown a straight red card for unsportsmanlike conduct, leaving the visitors to fight with ten men. Clinical Finish at the Velodrome With the numerical advantage, Marseille began to dismantle the opposition. In the 68th minute, a VAR review resulted in a penalty for a foul in the box. Amine Gouiri stepped up and coolly converted his second goal of the night, sending Filip Joergensen the wrong way. As the clock ticked down, the hosts introduced fresh legs, including Keyliane Abdallah , who made an immediate impact by finding the net in the 89th minute with a precise left-footed strike. Stoppage Time Fireworks The drama didn't end there. In the dying moments of stoppage time, Pierre-Emile Hoejbjerg produced a moment of magic, firing a right-footed shot from outside the box into the back of the net to make it 4-0 in the 96th minute. It was a statement performance from Marseille , who controlled 67% of the possession and efficiently exploited their man advantage to secure a comprehensive victory in front of their home supporters. Match Facts Scorers: Amine Gouiri (46', 68' PEN), Keyliane Abdallah (89'), Pierre-Emile Hoejbjerg (90+6'). Dismissals: Samir El Mourabet (Strasbourg) - 59th minute. Possession: Marseille 67% - 33% Strasbourg."
